{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB12874 - MONDO_17893",
  "verbalization": "Quizartinib is associated with Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia through a series of indirect pathways, primarily through the Npm1 somatic mutation in Acute Myeloid Leukemia. The evidence suggests that Quizartinib is indicated for Acute Myeloid Leukemia with Npm1 mutations, which in turn is linked to Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia via the indication for Ivosidenib and Mitoxantrone. While the direct relationship between Quizartinib and Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia is not explicitly stated, the shared pathway through Acute Myeloid Leukemia with Npm1 mutations implies a potential mechanistic link. The evidence supports a hypothesis that Quizartinib may act through a mechanism that is relevant to the treatment of Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia, possibly through targeting pathways involving Npm1 mutations. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Npm1 mutations in the context of Acute Myeloid Leukemia and suggests that Quizartinib may have a role in the management of this condition.",
